  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bbpcho/primitive-357-proof-audit/zipball/replay-companion-2026-09-15.2",
  "body": "This replacement restores a public replay package for Peter Chocian's first-submission paper on the primitive equation `x^3+y^5=z^7`.\n\nThe companion passed a fresh extraction and complete declared replay under an operating-system boundary that blocked network access and earlier proof-workspace reads: **13 sector/interface records, 65 prior jobs, 16 rank-local checks and five freshly generated input joins**. Five adapted archive readers (V2–V6) also passed separate default-entry-point checks. The main irreducible-sector mode remains `DEEP_REPLAY=0`; the records do not claim every optional historical search was reexecuted.\n\nThe revised 40-page paper prints this companion's actual checksum and tag in Section 8.5. Section 8.4 states the recorded Magma group flags and generator checks; PDF keyword metadata is filled. The small arXiv source ZIP contains only `manuscript.tex` and `rank-proof.tex`. A clean extraction of that ZIP reproduced the delivered PDF byte for byte. **The large companion stays on GitHub; it is not part of the arXiv source upload.**\n\nRequired third-party papers and unlicensed upstream source snapshots are acquired privately from pinned sources and checked against exact hashes. The public companion includes the input map, acquisition and reconstruction tools, original evidence, retained licensed material and the completed execution records. It excludes the identified unlicensed full-paper and source payloads. Read `FINAL_COMPANION_REPLAY_GUIDE.md` for the exact acquisition, runtime and replay instructions.\n\nThe additional V5 replay exposed a reporting typo: its eight exact support tables total **237,182 rows**, while historical aggregate labels say 236,182. All eight generated-set comparisons pass with no missing or extra rows. The companion preserves the tested source and raw logs and includes an explicit corrected summary and erratum.\n\nThe seven earlier Magma executions remain separately identified evidence; they were not rerun by this suite. The proof continues to depend on its cited mathematical results and computer-algebra algorithms. Successful replay does not constitute proof-assistant formalization or external human peer review.\n\n**No arXiv submission has been made. Dahmen's requested reply remains pending.** The release tag identifies the repository snapshot prepared before uploading; subsequent public-download and withdrawal observations are recorded in the [main-branch replacement audit](https://github.com/bbpcho/primitive-357-proof-audit/tree/main/audit/replacement-release-2026-09-15).\n\nCompanion: `PRIMITIVE_357_REPLAY_COMPANION_2026-09-15_V2.zip` (320731221 bytes)\n\nSHA-256: `a7e8308e906ab21410a18748e7b253518b26892aeab374baae7044407b164d85`\n\n`SHA256SUMS.txt` authenticates the companion, paper PDF, source ZIP and guide. Original code is MIT licensed; the original paper and documentation are CC BY 4.0, with third-party material explicitly excluded from those grants.\n"
